I am a biostatistics PhD student at Southern Methodist University (SMU) and a graduate research assistant in the Concussion, Acquired Brain Injury, and Neurodegeneration (CABIN) laboratory at UT Southwestern Medical Center. Prior to my PhD studies, I studied statistics (B.S.) and economics (B.A.) at SMU. My research interests include modeling noisy data, the intersection of machine learning and brain trauma research, and longitudinal analysis.

**Skills and Coursework:** Coding in R, Python, SAS, SQL; Bayesian Statistics; Clinical Trials; Linear Regression
